  "body": "The WPT test [cookieStore_get_arguments](https://wpt.fyi/results/cookie-store/cookieStore_get_arguments.https.any.html) includes a case for paths with fragments, which Chrome and Edge fail but Firefox passes. \n\nThe behavior in the spec for testing the path says to use [url-concept-equals](https://url.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-url-equals) where exclude fragments defaults to false. \n\nIt appears either the test is incorrect (though I believe this would not match the expected semantics of cookies, which the RFC seems to scope to just comparing the path portion of the URI) or the spec needs to specify that the URL equals needs to be performed with exclude fragements set to true.",
